{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And the man whom YHWH shall choose.</b> But did they not know this? Rather, thus he said: I am warning you not to obligate yourselves, for you shall know that the incense offering is beloved before the Holy One, blessed be He, more than all the sacrifices, and in it is placed the death potion — by it Nadav and Avihu were burned, and whoever the Holy One, blessed be He, chooses from among you is holy, that is, he will emerge alive, while all of you are doomed. Even so, they accepted the warning upon themselves and offered. As it is said: ״החטאים האלה בנפשותם״ — for he had already warned them. And if you ask: Korah, who was a wise man, what did he see to do such folly? His eye misled him, for he saw a great chain issuing from him, as Rashi z\"l explained, etc. And further, he expounded: 'I am ben Yitzhar' — as it is said: ״תירושך ויצהרך״ — tirosh, this is wine; yitzhar, this is oil. And with all liquids, when you put oil into them, the oil rises to the top. If so, it is fitting for him to be above all of them. And not only that, but it is said: ״ואלה בני היצהר״ — are there sons of oil? Rather, these are Aaron and David, who were anointed with the anointing oil: Aaron took the priesthood and David took the kingship. If these, who were anointed only with oil alone, took priesthood and kingship, then I, who am the son of the oil — is it not right that I be High Priest or king? Immediately he disputed with Moses."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:36.161738081Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}